---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["Can I use DMARC without SPF?", "Yes, if DKIM passes and aligns. But using both SPF and DKIM provides better coverage."], ["Does SPF stop email spoofing?", "Partially. SPF prevents IP spoofing but not header spoofing. DMARC closes that gap by requiring alignment with the From header."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "SPF vs DMARC",
  description: "SPF vs DMARC: SPF authorizes IPs, DMARC sets policy and reports. DMARC requires SPF or DKIM to pass first.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Can I use DMARC without SPF?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Yes, if DKIM passes and aligns. But using both SPF and DKIM provides better coverage." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Does SPF stop email spoofing?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Partially. SPF prevents IP spoofing but not header spoofing. DMARC closes that gap by requiring alignment with the From header." } },
    {'@type': 'Question', 'name': "Why does my mail pass SPF and still fail DMARC?", "acceptedAnswer": { '@type': 'Answer', "text": "Because SPF validated the envelope domain, which did not align with the visible From header. DMARC tests alignment; SPF alone cannot provide it." } }
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "SPF vs DMARC" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SPF vs DMARC: What Each Protocol Does and Why DMARC Requires SPF"
  description="SPF vs DMARC: SPF authorizes IPs, DMARC sets policy and reports. DMARC requires SPF or DKIM to pass first."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">SPF vs DMARC</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">SPF vs DMARC</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">SPF vs DMARC: SPF authorizes IPs, DMARC sets policy and reports. DMARC requires SPF or DKIM to pass.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'></th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>SPF</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>DMARC</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>RFC</td><td>7208</td><td>7489</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>What it does</td><td>Authorizes sending IP addresses</td><td>Defines enforcement policy and reporting</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>DNS record</td><td>TXT at root: v=spf1 ...</td><td>TXT at _dmarc: v=DMARC1; p=...</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Stops spoofing?</td><td>Only for IPs not in the record</td><td>Yes (enforces SPF/DKIM results)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Provides reports?</td><td>No</td><td>Yes (rua= aggregate reports)</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>Requires other protocols?</td><td>No</td><td>Yes (needs SPF or DKIM to pass)</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>SPF and DMARC are sequential email authentication protocols: SPF (RFC 7208) authorizes sending IP addresses via a DNS TXT record, while DMARC (RFC 7489) builds on those results to enforce a policy and generate reports.</p><p class='mt-3'>DMARC cannot function without SPF or DKIM: it requires at least one of those protocols to pass and align with the From header domain before it can apply its policy.</p><p class='mt-3'>SPF alone provides IP authorization but no enforcement or reporting: DMARC adds the policy layer (p=none, quarantine, reject) and the aggregate reporting mechanism (rua=).</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The progression I always recommend: SPF first (authorize your IPs), then DKIM (forward-safe authentication), then DMARC (enforcement + visibility). Each layer builds on the previous one.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I use DMARC without SPF?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes, if DKIM passes and aligns. But using both SPF and DKIM provides better coverage.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does SPF stop email spoofing?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Partially. SPF prevents IP spoofing but not header spoofing. DMARC closes that gap by requiring alignment with the From header.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why does my mail pass SPF and still fail DMARC?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Because SPF validated the envelope domain, which did not align with the visible From header. DMARC tests alignment; SPF alone cannot provide it.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
